2186045417] [17592186111757 #edb/ref 1061 9129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111757 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b8b06f5-4b02-515a-b65f-2c8a74aeac87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111757 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111758 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111758 #edb/ref 1061 9130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111758 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22624b6a-7b76-5955-88d7-2768f50c463e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111758 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111759 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111759 #edb/ref 1061 9132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111759 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0cffc650-bf34-5697-9746-2b68e2f3da89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111759 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111760 #edb/ref 1061 9134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111760 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "81bb680b-a34b-5ad8-9b3f-f51aa2a0acc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111760 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111843 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following triangle, where the side ![](images/72/721aa9559f1b9f3da3e69b1b9763327e29a6f3fb77157f4b42dd076d3865e098.svg) has been extended beyond the vertex ![](images/27/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg)\n\n![](images/6b/6be676cc487d17815701f3783e9eca71d7491a0e63d7ae9016fb65ad801e61d6.png)\n\n  \n\nThe resulting angle ![](images/f1/f1729f131b4ec04b45c992a99498753dd09d27e76e917dff66d1fd554ec2ab5e.svg) is called the **exterior angle** at vertex ![](images/27/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg) \n\nExterior angles have the following properties:\n\n- An exterior angle and its corresponding interior angle form a linear pair and are therefore supplementary. Here, we have\n![](images/9a/9ae2a4aa323b941eff72a50f5c1086c72e961d0eed919a327306e77cfd5a7ef6.svg)\n\n- The measure of an exterior angle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two non-adjacent interior angles. This is called the **exterior angles theorem**. To see why it is true, notice that since the internal angles of a triangle sum to ![](images/1a/1ace39b6f52fbf0b8654fc88bfa3e97366d33e3c411580da106e513a498aca53.svg) we have \n![](images/49/49aafbdb975ccd101e16c921c20630af6296b860438ebfb62d8a205cc6e7b3c7.svg)\n\n- At each vertex of a triangle, there are two exterior angles. They are vertical angles, and consequently, they have the same measure.\n\n![](images/b4/b459ad1edd5e0fdf512d722eb55ab20ff66c281d7160077d12936a6926529aa0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111843 #edb/ref 1065 2223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111843 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d29b69d0-268e-57ed-9c22-289173b3c810" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111843 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111844 #edb/ref 1064 "Yet another important fact about exterior angles is:\n\nThe sum of the measures of the exterior angles of a triangle is always equal to $360^\\circ.$\n\nSo, for the triangle below, we have \n\n$$\nx+y+z = 360^\\circ.\n$$\n\n![](images/22/22586791e1118a38a554deffaec3ac5b73eafc47eee4be2052c0949dde584cea.png)\n\nTo see why, first recall that the measure of an exterior angle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two non-adjacent interior angles. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =m∠B+m∠C \\\\ y & =m∠A+m∠C \\\\ z & =m∠A+m∠B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that the internal angles of a triangle sum to $180^\\circ.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & =(m∠B+m∠C)+(m∠A+m∠C)+(m∠A+m∠B) \\\\  & =2m∠A+2m∠B+2m∠C \\\\  & =2(m∠A+m∠B+m∠C) \\\\  & =2({180}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111844 #edb/ref 1065 2226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111844 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3f605c56-a279-51cc-be43-72f1b9030f58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111844 #edb/ref 1067 "The Sum of Exterior Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505180 #edb/ref 1080 "{52}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505180 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505180 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2a2e21a4-7ffd-5db7-81d7-cae99b955de3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505183 #edb/ref 1080 "{35}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ab03a6b-b7a6-52e5-a099-6438918f7051" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505201 #edb/ref 1080 "{55}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505201 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505201 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "366c1c43-d53f-58eb-8483-cd45c87c0df1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505206 #edb/ref 1080 "{147}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505206 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505206 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39fd7c9e-0ea0-51fd-96cb-49ea653f5205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505279 #edb/ref 1080 "{51}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505279 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505279 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56a0ec06-e947-55b9-8faf-8159c782df26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505288 #edb/ref 1080 "{70}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b0fe1f2-d6a9-56e5-a21a-230a23f1a790" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505292 #edb/ref 1080 "{155}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505292 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505292 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ca05c0c-36e6-59da-9e50-1878055139fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505300 #edb/ref 1080 "{46}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505300 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505300 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "60d2dd30-298a-557e-bc40-f2d7d3620958" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505315 #edb/